The claim is supported by data from Macrotrends, which uses World Bank and UN Population Division estimates, showing Nigeria's urban population in 2020 was approximately 52.5%, closely aligning with the stated 52%. While a 2022 estimate from the [World Bank](https://tradingeconomics.com/nigeria/urban-population-percent-of-total-wb-data.html) is slightly higher at 53.52%, this does not contradict the 2020 figure, and the international demographic sources consistently corroborate an urbanization rate of around half the population at that time.